+<h2>121. Two comments in the certify route no longer say that writing the row first removes the orphan-anchor window, or that the under-claim lasts a sub-second (KS-1666 note d)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td>Two comment blocks in <code>Blockchain/Dev/services/originate/src/routes/certifications.ts</code> (lines 520 and 527 at the base), +4/-2. The first said that writing the <code>documents</code> row before the anchor &ldquo;removes the window rather than narrowing it&rdquo;. It now says it <strong>narrows</strong> the window: when the reservation itself fails, the anchor-then-fail path is unchanged. The second called the provisional row&rsquo;s under-claim a &ldquo;sub-second window&rdquo;. It now says the window runs until the second write, is bounded by the anchoring call&rsquo;s <code>AbortSignal.timeout(10000)</code>, and so is up to 10 seconds. <strong>No executable line moves.</strong></td></tr><tr><td>New test <code>ks1666-certify-reservation-comments-match-the-code.test.ts</code>, 5 cells, reading <code>certifications.ts</code> as text: R1 and R2 are RED until the two comments are corrected; C1 to C3 are controls (the 10000 ms bound is still in the code, the code still says an orphan anchor can be created when the reservation fails, the file was read). This is note (d) of the ticket only; the ticket carries nine gate notes and this change covers none of the others.</td></tr></table>
+<h3>121.1 What proves it</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>Red before the change, green after, and no other cell moves.</strong></td><td><strong>Test only, at develop <code>a786e06e6f6e</code>:</strong> 2 of 5 cells fail (R1, R2) and the 3 controls pass. <strong>With the two comments corrected:</strong> 5 of 5 pass.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Comment-only proof:</strong> the base file and the changed file, transpiled with TypeScript 5.9.3 with comments removed, are identical (53,964 bytes of output). A control copy with one code token changed (<code>signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10000),</code> to 10001) is not identical to the base. All 6 changed lines of <code>git diff -U0</code> are <code>//</code> lines. The first run of this control targeted the first <code>AbortSignal.timeout(10000)</code>, which sits in the new comment, so it could not fire; it was corrected to the code line and the first output is kept.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Whole originate unit suite</strong> (jest 29.7.0, <code>--maxWorkers=3</code>): 152 files, 1854 cells, 1854 pass, 0 fail, 0 skipped, 48 s. The checker&rsquo;s untouched-tip figure was 1849 cells at <code>593cd90c3131</code>; it was not re-measured at <code>a786e06e6f6e</code>. <code>tsc --noEmit</code> with <code>src/__tests__</code> in the program (232 originate source files, 175 under <code>__tests__</code>): <strong>0 errors</strong>, and a planted type error was reported once as <code>TS2322</code> by file name. <code>eslint</code> on the new test file: 0 errors, 0 warnings, and a planted file raised <code>@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars</code> and <code>no-debugger</code>.</td></tr></table>
+<h3>121.2 Environment and figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Where and when this was measured.</strong></td><td>Measured 2026-10-29 (UTC) on an Apple Silicon (arm64) Mac, macOS 27.0.1, shared with other seats. Node v26.8.1 (not an LTS line), TypeScript 5.9.3, jest 29.7.0, ts-jest 29.4.14, eslint 10.7.0.</td></tr></table>
+<h3>121.3 What this does not prove</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>Stated, not claimed.</strong></td><td>The claim in the new comment that the window is up to 10 seconds. This change reads the code (at the base: the provisional write at line 577, the anchoring <code>fetch</code> with the 10000 ms signal at lines 598 to 616, the authoritative save at line 673) and does not time it. The bound is the anchoring call&rsquo;s; the two database writes around it are not included.</td></tr><tr><td>Not run: the originate integration files (they need a database), the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a running stack, Node 24, any deploy. The pre-push hook&rsquo;s leg count is stated in the pull request.</td></tr></table>
+<h3>121.4 Running it</h3>
+<pre><code>cd Blockchain/Dev/services/originate &amp;&amp; npm test -- ks1666-certify-reservation-comments   # 5 cells, rc 0
+cd Blockchain/Dev/services/originate &amp;&amp; npm test -- --maxWorkers=3                           # 152 files / 1854 cells, rc 0</code></pre>
